# SSR and runtime environment

Runtime packages are consumed by SSR frameworks (`exporters-next`, `exporters-nuxt`, Angular SSR). Components must be **SSR-safe where practical**; heavy client-only components must ship an explicit guard and placeholder.

## Universal rules

- **No `window`, `document`, `localStorage`, or `navigator` at module top level** — access only inside lifecycle/mount/effect after an environment check.
- **Guard pattern:**

```ts
const isBrowser = typeof globalThis !== 'undefined' && typeof document !== 'undefined';
```

- **Custom element registration** — call `registerRd*()` in mount/effect/first render, not at import time (except idempotent no-op guards inside register).
- **Dynamic import** heavy deps: `three`, `@ffmpeg/ffmpeg`, map SDKs — never static-import at module scope in SSR entry paths.

## SSR-safe components (default expectation)

Layout, inputs, charts (static SVG/canvas-free), KPI, table, news, domain atoms — render meaningful HTML on server with correct `rd-*` structure and ARIA.

## Client-only components (allowed with guard)

| Category | Examples | Requirement |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| Media CEs | `video-source`, `equirect-viewport`, `wasm/media` | Render placeholder `<div>` or host tag on server; mount CE in browser |
| 3D / maps | `3d-geo-globe`, `geo-map`, three hosts | Placeholder + `aria-label`; hydrate scene client-side |
| WASM / ffmpeg | `WasmMedia` | No wasm init on server |
| Live capture | `live-capture` | Guard `getUserMedia` |

Client-only components must export or document:

1. **`ssr: false`** in README row (convention until typed metadata exists)
2. Server placeholder with same dimensions (`minHeight` prop honored)
3. No throw on import in Node — defer failure to mount

## Framework notes

| Runtime | Mount hook |
|---------|------------|
| React | `useEffect`; guard StrictMode double-mount (dispose in cleanup) |
| Vue | `onMounted` |
| Angular | `ngOnInit` / `afterNextRender` |
| Svelte | `$effect` with `onMount` cleanup |
| WC | `connectedCallback` / `disconnectedCallback` |

## Storage and persistence

See `32-storage-and-persistence.mdc` — all storage access behind browser guard; SSR returns defaults.

## COOP/COEP (media apps)

Proof apps and media demos requiring SharedArrayBuffer must set headers at app level — not inside components. Document in app README, not in atom code.

## Checklist

- [ ] Module import does not throw in Node
- [ ] Browser APIs only after guard
- [ ] Heavy deps dynamically imported
- [ ] `disconnectedCallback` / effect cleanup disposes listeners, RAF, object URLs
- [ ] Client-only components have SSR placeholder documented

